      "value": "I was thinking about the potential abuse vector of community worlds that ban people from the world entirely, but the more I think about it the more of a non-issue I think it is on a large scale? Requiring people to join your group before seeing and accessing an otherwise public world would absolutely destroy discoverability, which would make it very hard to grow and maintain a community, so it's only really feasible for very niche edge cases, and I think that mostly resolves the issue.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
